        {
          "id": 1310847161,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> There are many/several/a few copies of `zlib1.dll` in my `wireshark-win64-libs` directory so without specifying the path, a random (and incorrect) copy is chosen?\n\nIs it just an incorrect guess? Or do you actually see any sort of randomness?\n\n`cmake/modules/FindZLIB.cmake` defines `ZLIB_INCLUDE_DIRS`, `ZLIB_LIBRARIES`, `ZLIB_DLL_DIR`, `ZLIB_DLL` and `ZLIB_PDB` (and a few others). `CMakeLists.txt` then does `list (APPEND THIRD_PARTY_DLLS \"${ZLIB_DLL_DIR}/${ZLIB_DLL}\")` and `list (APPEND THIRD_PARTY_PDBS \"${ZLIB_DLL_DIR}/${ZLIB_PDB}\")`. There is no randomness whatsoever and if the file is not copied for whatever reason, then the `cmake/modules/FindZLIB.cmake` should be fixed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e423f0a8da1eede7f89748e5142d6915e4a636399964d35d888ed95ca85e2b50?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/desowin"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-03-13T06:14:14.693Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-03-13T06:14:14.693Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 210666119,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
